            <ArticleTitle>A case of ectopic cilia.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>297-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1007/s10792-008-9228-0</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Ectopic cilia are the most rare of cilial anomalies. We report a 27-year-old man who presents with tarsal conjunctival symptomatic ectopic cilia. On slit-lamp examination eversion of the lower eyelid demonstrated that several black-white cilia were protruding from the conjunctiva.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
